{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae20-8568-7b60-9562-eee7c66138af"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260917-3lt2xv, status=reviewing)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `reviewer` (`reviewer`) — Reviews implementation quality and project fit\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] cataloggen -adopted derives metadata/lock from catalog.Adopted, is byte-identical to the explicit invocation, and refuses mixed flags, missing inputs and a lock whose release differs from the adopted release\n- [ ] Validation command 21 uses the -adopted form; trunk's explicit command and the new form are both green on the candidate; no catalog content or generated output changes\n- [ ] README/LOGBOOK document the release-agnostic gate without capability claims\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n- [ ] Implementation matches AC\n- [ ] Solution fits project architecture\n- [ ] Tests green\n- [ ] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\n- [ ] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260917-3lt2xv\n- **Title:** TASK-260917-3lt2xv: make-cataloggen-check-release-agnostic\n- **Parent:** STORY-260917-158jyi\n\n### Description\n\nAdd an adopted-release mode to cataloggen that derives the catalog metadata and normative lock inputs from the code-level current release, switch validation command 21 in task-board.config.json to that form, and prove byte-identical output against the explicit invocation plus refusals for missing or mismatched inputs.\n\n### Scope\n\ninternal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen, internal/cataloggen, internal/catalog (read-only consumers of Current/ForRelease), task-board.config.json command 21, README tool row, LOGBOOK.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\ngo run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check exits 0 on trunk and produces byte-identical output to the explicit v0.6.0 invocation; explicit -metadata/-contracts still work and mixing them with -adopted is refused; a missing metadata or lock file for the current release, or a lock whose release differs from the current release, is refused with a distinct message; task-board.config.json command 21 is the -adopted form; every other validation command unchanged; tests drive the production main through its entry with positives and refusals and a narrowing mutant per refusal; no catalog content or generated output changes.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260917-3lt2xv/TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4433`\n- Content digest: `sha256:408cce1ee47953998468ff9ebfda3947cddb0fd308563aa14cb74fff96108b79`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260917-3lt2xv_reviewer-cr1.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260917-3lt2xv/TASK-260917-3lt2xv_reviewer-cr1.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4683`\n- Content digest: `sha256:c62487f97412aa8e1ed50ec7601ecbcd51e1b65567f55fd1fba2cf1915d82f41`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260917-3lt2xv_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260917-3lt2xv, name=TASK-260917-3lt2xv_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- You are licensed to attempt to DEFEAT any gate, refusal, validation, authorization, or attestation under review, and to reject a change whose only evidence is positive-path. Grep for callers before believing a guard is in force; a delete-only mutant proves existence, not coverage.\n- Review read-only and record exactly one evidence-backed verdict: accepted → `done`; changes requested → `to-dev` or `analysis`; genuine Stop-The-Line → `blocked`. Never leave the task in `reviewing`.\n- With a `Change Request Under Review` section, accept via `task-board m 'accept_cr(ID, revision=N, evidence=ID_review-verdict.md)'`. It writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically and routes the element to `integrating` — accepted work never stays in `reviewing` and never reaches `done` from here. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype; only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it, and the orchestrator routes that run but does not close the leaf. `accept_cr` takes no acknowledgement argument, and only the reviewer run that was handed the revision may call it.\n- Reviewer-archetype runs must not supply `commit_ack` and must not escalate the commit-or-acknowledge decision to the human; record acceptance evidence and leave every `done` transition to the producer side.\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260917-158jyi.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260917-158jyi/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260917-158jyi`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n\n## Change Request Under Review\n\n- Change Request: `CR-TASK-260917-3lt2xv-1` revision `1` (state `ready`)\n- Element: `TASK-260917-3lt2xv`, integration scope: `STORY-260917-158jyi`\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260917-158jyi`\n- Base OID: `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e`\n- Candidate tree OID: `83e6eb6f27f5d31ce313873e6a0f7104fefbee9a`\n- Repository delta: `present`\n- Patch resource: `TASK-260917-3lt2xv_change-request_rev1.patch` (sha256 `0ed4c9efdaeb1ac89a3e2a5b931745afa13b81d64e9517512f972916da563499`)\n\n```bash\ngit -C . diff 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e 83e6eb6f27f5d31ce313873e6a0f7104fefbee9a          # the exact reviewable delta\ngit -C . diff --stat 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e 83e6eb6f27f5d31ce313873e6a0f7104fefbee9a   # its shape\n```\n\nChanged paths (7):\n\n- `LOGBOOK.md`\n- `README.md`\n- `internal/catalog/catalog.go`\n- `internal/catalog/catalog_test.go`\n- `internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen/main.go`\n- `internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen/main_test.go`\n- `task-board.config.json`\n\n### Recording the verdict\n\nAcceptance is a named mutation, not a status change:\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'accept_cr(TASK-260917-3lt2xv, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260917-3lt2xv_review-verdict-rev1.md)'\n```\n\n`accept_cr` writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically: the Change Request becomes `accepted`, this run is stamped as the reviewer, and TASK-260917-3lt2xv routes the element to `integrating` — accepted but not landed, and never `done`. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype (`developer`/`implementer`), and only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it. The orchestrator routes that run; it does not close the leaf, and no orchestrator run may execute the integration itself. `done` is produced only by the integration transaction, never by you and never by an acknowledgement. Never supply `commit_ack` yourself.\n\nChanges requested and Stop-The-Line are unchanged: route to `to-dev`/`analysis` or evidence-backed `blocked`. Leaving the element in `reviewing` is still not a verdict and still gets this run cancelled and respawned.\n"}}
