{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c409","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae20-8568-7b60-9562-eee7c66138af"},"sequence":95,"recorded_at":1780531400000185,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae20-cc86-7953-9f6a-a4eb0e66da4b"},"task_id":"01a0ae20-cc86-7953-9f6a-a4eb0e66da4b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae20-cc86-7953-9f6a-a4eb0e66da4b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-2-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls -R /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260917-3lt2xv/ 2>&1; echo \\\"---\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260917-3lt2xv/TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer.md; echo \\\"===REVIEWER-CR1===\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260917-3lt2xv/TASK-260917-3lt2xv_reviewer-cr1.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read attached task docs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer.md\\nTASK-260917-3lt2xv_reviewer-cr1.md\\n---\\nOwn TASK-260917-3lt2xv (make-cataloggen-check-release-agnostic), the single leaf of STORY-260917-158jyi (release-agnostic-catalog-validation-gate) under EPIC-260916-18uelk. Why: Change Request construction runs the CONTROL ROOT's configured validation suite against a candidate; validation command 21 is today `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`, so a Story that re-points the catalog to a newly pinned revision (TASK-260916-n9r71p for v0.7.0 right now; CR-TASK-260916-n9r71p-1 failed at command 21 with \\\"normative source pin mismatch: source identity drift\\\"; the v0.6.0 adoption hit the same collision, see TASK-260908-2tkufa_integration-outcome.md) can never pass construction, because its own cataloggen correctly refuses the stale lock. Fix the contract at the source, not with a workaround: (1) declare the adopted release once in internal/catalog (for example `const Adopted Release = ReleaseV060` next to Current(), with Current() defined through it so the two cannot diverge; add a test pinning Current().Release == Adopted); (2) add an `-adopted` mode to internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen that derives `-metadata internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `-contracts internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` from catalog.Adopted relative to a `-root` (default \\\".\\\" — the validation suite runs from the repository root), refuses `-adopted` combined with explicit -metadata/-contracts, refuses a missing metadata or lock file with distinct messages naming the derived path, refuses a lock whose source release differs from the adopted release before generation, and otherwise behaves byte-identically to the explicit invocation (same Generate call, same -check/-output semantics); (3) switch validation command 21 in task-board.config.json to `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` (edit exactly that string in the candidate; never edit the control root; every other command unchanged) and prove it green on the candidate; (4) README tool row for cataloggen documents the -adopted form and the explicit form; LOGBOOK entry. No catalog content, metadata, lock or generated-output change: `git diff --exit-code internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json internal/specpin/` must be empty. Tests drive the production entry (the cataloggen run function / main through os/exec) with positives (-adopted -check green; -adopted generation byte-identical to explicit generation into a temp output; explicit flags still work) and refusals (mixed flags; missing metadata; missing lock; lock release != adopted via a temp root with a v0.5.0 lock copied under the adopted name; stale generated output under -adopted -check), a narrowing mutant per refusal and per the byte-identity claim with a shipped harness (per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control), and a conformance row map to the task AC. Managed Story worktree contract: the worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/STORY-260917-158jyi/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260917-158jyi forked from current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260917-3lt2xv and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). This is the Story's only leaf, so the CR is story_final. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff (your candidate's command 21 and trunk's explicit command 21 must BOTH be green on your tree — construction will run trunk's); hand off no later than 1.5 hours in. Attach TASK-260917-3lt2xv_results.md, TASK-260917-3lt2xv_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260917-3lt2xv --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.\\n===REVIEWER-CR1===\\nIndependently review Change Request revision 1 of TASK-260917-3lt2xv (make-cataloggen-check-release-agnostic, the single leaf of STORY-260917-158jyi — story_final: story_final on trunk base 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e with the checkpointed predecessor commits  on the Story branch (tip 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e), published by RUN-260917-b2cfa8 on muse-spark max, 7 changed paths in the whole-Story patch, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260917-3lt2xv_change-request_rev1.patch / _rev1-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer.md (it states why: CR construction runs the control-root suite, and a catalog re-point Story such as TASK-260916-n9r71p cannot pass explicit v0.6.0 command 21), the outcome TASK-260917-3lt2xv_results.md, TASK-260917-3lt2xv_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260917-3lt2xv_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes.\\n\\nVerify with your own instruments: (1) Contract — catalog.Adopted is the single declaration and Current() is defined through it (plant a divergence: set Current() to ForRelease(ReleaseV050) while Adopted stays v0.6.0 — the pin test must go RED); `-adopted` derives exactly internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json and internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json under -root and calls the same Generate path as the explicit form: generate both into temp outputs from an isolated copy and cmp them byte-for-byte; run `-adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` and the explicit trunk command on the candidate tree — both exit 0; run `-adopted` from a temp root where the adopted metadata is missing, where the lock is missing, where the lock under the adopted name is actually the v0.5.0 lock (release mismatch), and with mixed `-adopted -metadata …` flags — each refused with the distinct message the results claim, and none of them writes the output file; confirm `-adopted -check` against a stale generated file fails exactly like the explicit form. (2) Forward proof — simulate the consumer this exists for: in an isolated copy set Adopted to a fake release with matching temp metadata/lock names copied from v0.6.0 (or use the v0.5.0 pair under v0.5.0 names) and confirm `-adopted` follows the declaration while the explicit v0.6.0 command still works; state precisely what the n9r71p candidate must do (set Adopted = ReleaseV070; keep command 21 untouched) for its construction to pass. (3) Config — JSON-walk the task-board.config.json diff: exactly the command-21 string changes, no model/signing/gate/trigger field; the candidate suite and trunk suite differ only in that command; forecast the integrate-time guard: evidence was produced under trunk's suite (construction) while the CR changes the suite — say whether validation_suite_changed can refuse and cite the guard code path if you can find it in the task-board source at /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management (read-only). (4) No content change — `git diff --exit-code` between trunk and the candidate for internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go, internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json, internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json and internal/specpin/ must be empty. (5) Mutation — rerun the producer harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, plant at least three narrowing mutants of your own (derive the lock path from the metadata's release instead of Adopted; skip the release-mismatch refusal when the file parses; accept mixed flags when -check is set) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) Docs and hygiene — README tool row and LOGBOOK truthful; changed_paths exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc, no stray plants; go vet, gofmt, go test ./internal/catalog/... ./internal/cataloggen -count=1 and -race green; the full 26-command suite green under the candidate command 21 on the exact tree.\\n\\nMethod: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260917-3lt2xv/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260917-3lt2xv_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260917-3lt2xv_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260917-3lt2xv, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260917-3lt2xv_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9205,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2302,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
