{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca81","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae20-8568-7b60-9562-eee7c66138af"},"sequence":923,"recorded_at":1780531400001841,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2c-4816-7fb0-bbed-225002aee24d"},"task_id":"01a0ae2c-4816-7fb0-bbed-225002aee24d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2c-4816-7fb0-bbed-225002aee24d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-36-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/ 2>&1 | head -n 20; grep -rn \\\"validation_suite_changed\\\" /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/ 2>&1 | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Search integrate-time guard code path\",\n  \"execution_state\": \"background_running\",\n  \"session_id\": 36,\n  \"work_id\": \"work.v1.managed_bash.sha256.2307e5f05964d32d57c762cbed72814499ee5048ad49740d69fc57c94398d6b3\",\n  \"model_guidance\": \"The command is still running in the background and the UI already shows its status. Do not poll for completion: the final output is delivered to you automatically as runtime context and wakes you even after you end the turn. Exception: when a runtime overdue notice names a still-running session, you may inspect it or terminate it with bash_input now. Do not narrate that it started, is running, shows current output, will continue, or has an internal session_id unless the user explicitly asks or you have substantive next work. If there is nothing else to do, end the turn without extra status text. Managed sessions end when your agent session ends, and this host is macOS, which does not ship `setsid` to detach with: if the deliverable is a process that must keep running after your final answer, say so and ask how to proceed.\",\n  \"output\": \"agent-skill.json\\narticles\\nCLAUDE.md\\ndiagrams\\ndocker-compose.coolify.yml\\ndocs\\nLICENSE\\nLOGBOOK.md\\nMakefile\\nNOTICE\\npkg\\nplanning\\nREADME.md\\nreferences\\nscripts\\nSKILL.md\\nSkillfile.json\\nSPEC.md\\ntask-board.config.json\\ntestdata\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/uncovered_gates_test.go:247:// `validation_suite_changed` — refuse outright.\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/integrate_matrix_test.go:220:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"error = %v, want validation_suite_changed\\\", err)\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/integrate_matrix_test.go:224:\\t\\tt.Fatal(\\\"HEAD moved on validation_suite_changed\\\")\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/errors.go:90:\\tErrorValidationSuiteChanged ErrorCode = \\\"validation_suite_changed\\\"\\nBinary file /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/task-board matches\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260720-1fjsu9_board-workflow-and-spawn-policy-enhancements/STORY-260721-3er9sm_per-story-worktree-isolation-for-spawn/TASK-260803-kpx06r_implement-safe-story-squash-integration/progress.md:23:- [x] Implement tree-bound validation: refuse validation_not_bound_to_tree, validation_not_passing, validation_suite_changed, and validation_not_configured before any ref movement\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260720-1fjsu9_board-workflow-and-spawn-policy-enhancements/STORY-260721-3er9sm_per-story-worktree-isolation-for-spawn/TASK-260803-kpx06r_implement-safe-story-squash-integration/README.md:10:1. Before the final unresolved leaf producer starts, a clean short-lived Story checkpoint branch is refreshed to current trunk; conflicts are persisted and routed to same-branch rework, while success records the reviewed trunk OID. 2. The final leaf CR covers the complete Story candidate tree and integration refuses unless the latest evidence-backed accepted revision, candidate tree, and branch match by CAS and current trunk either equals reviewed_trunk_oid or re-parents onto it under AC 6. 3. task-board worktree integrate is orchestrator-only and creates exactly one single-parent commit with message keyed to Story plus CR, using repository Git identity and the accepted candidate tree; trunk advances only by ff-only. 4. Internal Task checkpoint commits are not preserved on trunk; no partial Story landing or application feature flag is allowed. 5. With version_control.confirm enabled, an explicit RFC3339 commit time is required, both author and committer dates equal it, the prose desired_commit_time and actual OID and time are recorded, and only post-Git board done uses commit_ack=scope_committed. 6. Acceptance invalidation is keyed to changed-path intersection, not trunk-OID equality. An intersecting advance routes to refresh, validation, and a new review revision. A non-intersecting advance re-parents in place through a three-way tree merge with base=base_oid, ours=trunk, theirs=candidate_tree_oid: a merge conflict, or a merged tree whose diff against trunk is not exactly changed_paths, demotes to stale; otherwise the CR keeps its revision and accepted state and emits a reparented audit event. A named test proves the accepted candidate tree is never committed under a moved trunk without that merge. 7. Validation evidence is bound to a tree OID, not to a CR and not to a commit. Integration refuses unless validation.tree_oid equals the candidate tree being committed (validation_not_bound_to_tree), validation.exit_status is zero (validation_not_passing), and validation.suite_sha256 equals the digest of the configured suite (validation_suite_changed). An unset worktree.validation.commands refuses with validation_not_configured before any ref movement; the gate defaults to refusing rather than to landing an unvalidated tree. 8. Because re-parenting sets a new candidate tree, it necessarily breaks the AC 7 binding and forces revalidation. A tree OID cannot be checked out: git worktree add --detach exits 128 with object is a tree, not a commit, reproduced on git 2.53.0. The merged tree is therefore materialized as the exact commit integration will land, by git commit-tree merged_tree -p trunk_oid with the resolved backdated author and committer dates; git rev-parse commit^{tree} must equal merged_tree; refs/task-board/revalidate/STORY-ID is created by an expected-old-value CAS against absent, both anchoring the commit against gc and refusing a leaked ref from a crashed attempt with revalidation_stale_ref rather than adopting it; the workspace is git worktree add --detach .temp/STORY-ID/revalidate at that commit; and the workspace HEAD^{tree} must equal merged_tree with a clean porcelain status before the suite runs. validation.tree_oid records merged_tree and never the materialized commit OID, which is retained as diagnostic context only. Teardown removes the workspace and deletes the ref on every exit path, and worktree gc prunes refs whose Story has no in-flight transaction plus any orphaned workspace. Revalidation runs inside the Story lease and the repository integration lock. Exit zero rebinds validation to the merged tree and preserves acceptance; a non-zero exit sets revalidation_failed and routes the element to to-dev with the log as an outcome resource, so the next handoff is a new CR revision requiring a new review; a suite or materialization that cannot execute sets revalidation_unavailable or revalidation_materialization_failed, neither of which is a pass or a rework signal, leaving integration blocked and retryable. revalidate_attempts is capped at 3 per accepted revision, after which the CR demotes to stale. When trunk has not moved again, trunk advances by ff-only to that same validated commit. 9. A named negative drives the real integrate entry point on a fixture where trunk advances with a signature change in path B while the accepted Story changes only its caller in path A, constructed so that path disjointness, the three-way merge, and the changed_paths equality check all pass. Validation must fail and the run must leave trunk unmoved, nothing staged in the control root, board status unchanged, no git_integrated_board_pending transaction phase, and the CR at revalidation_failed. 10. The class is proven by narrowing, not by deletion. Rebinding the AC 7 precondition from validation.tree_oid to validation.cr_id plus revision must make the AC 9 negative fail. Additionally, deriving validation.tree_oid from the materialized workspace's own HEAD^{tree} instead of asserting equality with merged_tree must make design matrix rows V1 and V2 fail: V1 pre-creates a stale refs/task-board/revalidate/STORY-ID pointing at an unrelated commit and requires revalidation_stale_ref with no suite run and no recorded pass; V2 makes materialization yield a workspace that is not the tree under test and requires revalidation_unavailable. A delete-only mutant is not accepted as evidence for any of these. 11. There is exactly ONE durable integration record, the IntegrationTxn keyed by story_id, cr_id and revision; the board write journal is a separate non-authorizing store-consistency mechanism that carries no integration phase and is never consulted by integration. The transaction is opened and fsynced in step 4, AFTER the phase-A closing re-read and STRICTLY BEFORE the step-5 ff-only trunk advance, which is the only irreversible act in the flow; step 1 builds the candidate commit through git commit-tree, which moves no ref. It carries the immutable identity story_id, cr_id, cr_revision, transition_element_id, expected_trunk_oid, candidate_tree_oid, candidate_commit_oid, repository_delta_empty, changed_paths, resolved_commit_time, phase_a_snapshot and precondition_delta, plus step6_write_set written once at sub-step 6b and refusal written at most once, and ONE monotonic NINE-phase ladder prepared, git_integrated_board_pending, board_transition_pending, transition_refused, integration_abandoned, board_state_pending, integrated, cleanup_pending, discharged, each advance fsynced before the next step. NO PHASE IS ENTERED ON THE STRENGTH OF THE RECORD THAT NAMES IT: entry to board_state_pending re-classifies lane_plan and refuses txn_transition_not_in_place into transition_refused on any residual PRE, and cleanup at discharged recomputes the AC 31 discharge postcondition, so a hand-written phase field is a resume point and never a credential. Design section 6.3.4d is the SINGLE NORMATIVE SOURCE for that ladder and its per-phase recovery; every other statement of it in the design or in this AC is a derived view and section 6.3.4d governs on any disagreement. Recovery dispatches on the recorded OIDs: phase prepared with trunk equal to expected_trunk_oid is rollback-or-resume with nothing landed; phase prepared with trunk equal to candidate_commit_oid is treated as git_integrated_board_pending and completed exactly once; any third trunk value refuses integration_indeterminate and never adopts, forces or guesses. Retry is idempotent across every phase and across duplicate invocation. A zero-repository-delta Story still opens the transaction in step 4 with repository_delta_empty true and candidate_commit_oid null, skipping only steps 1 to 3 and step 5. 12. Cleanup removes the short-lived worktree and branch only after exact commit ancestry, Story done, a committed board record, clean workspace, and no active lease or RUN; force removal or deletion is never automatic. 13. The integration checkout is the control root and no other checkout is ever advanced. Integration refuses with typed evidence unless the control root is the repository main working tree, HEAD is attached, HEAD names the configured trunk branch, HEAD equals the reviewed OID, the trunk branch is checked out in no other linked worktree, and no merge, rebase or cherry-pick is in progress. A named test asserts that a control root whose HEAD is an ancestor of trunk on a side branch is refused rather than fast-forwarded. 14. After the board mutation, integrate commits the Story board delta as a second board-only commit in the control root titled Record STORY-ID board state, carrying the same resolved backdated timestamp, created by an ordinary git commit on the control root whose HEAD already names trunk, staged by an explicit pathspec of exactly the manifest paths and never by git add -A or a prefix glob. 15. This task owns orchestrator-computed board-path admission. For each candidate path under board_paths(STORY-ID): a path present in the worktree is admitted only when a live element owns it and its bytes equal the store's current rendering, else board_path_content_unrecognized; a path absent but tracked in HEAD is admitted only when no live element owns it, else board_path_content_unrecognized; a shared-plane path must be present, else board_shared_plane_delete; a path also in changed_paths refuses with board_code_overlap; gitignored untracked paths are skipped. Refusal is integration-wide, listing every offending path and reason, with nothing staged, nothing committed, and no board mutation replayed; paths outside board_paths(STORY-ID) are not examined, staged, or committed. No child-authored record, environment variable, working directory, or caller-supplied field is consulted, and board_delta_unattested and board_delta_foreign_lane do not exist. Design matrix row P1 is mandatory and is the regression that architecture revision 7 failed: a real producer run, accept_cr and integrate must SUCCEED, with trunk gaining the Story commit and the board-only commit, the element reaching done, and the leaf, Story and Epic progress writes step 6 caused all present in the board commit. 16. The integration-window CAS is phase-aware and lane-class only, because step 6 is required to change exactly the paths the window protects, and its phase-B bound is DURABLE rather than in-process. Phase A snapshots sha256 of every lane path at integration-lock acquisition and re-reads them in step 4, immediately before the transaction opens and therefore strictly before the step-5 trunk advance, refusing board_delta_moved on any difference; the refusal must leave trunk unmoved and no transaction record on disk, and a closing read placed after the ff-only advance is a defect because it makes those postconditions unreachable. Phase A covers steps 1 to 4; a lane write landing during step 5 is caught by phase B, so the window is guarded end to end. Step 6 runs as four ordered sub-steps under one held board mutation lock: 6a plans the write set, 6b fsyncs it into the transaction as step6_write_set and advances the phase to board_transition_pending BEFORE the mutation writes any byte, 6c applies the status mutation and makes TWO assertions that are not redundant, first that the returned path set equals the path projection of step6_write_set, which is the only one that can see an EXTRA written path, and second that the store now renders post_digest for every LANE entry of step6_write_set, which is the only one that survives the process, and 6d fsyncs the advance to board_state_pending and releases the transition lease. Either assertion failing is txn_write_set_divergence, which MUST be fsynced as refusal with phase transition_refused BEFORE it is reported. Phase B holds that lock through the freeze, re-derives the expected post-state from the store, and requires the set of lane paths whose expected post-state differs from the phase A snapshot to be a SUBSET of txn.step6_write_set read from the durable record, refusing board_delta_moved otherwise. EVERY phase-B evaluation, live or reached by crash recovery, reads that same durable field; binding phase B to an in-process return value is the architecture revision 9 defect, because a crash after the transition became durable then left the resumed freeze with no bound and admitted in-window drift through precondition_delta. Substituting step6_projection(txn) on the recovery path is also a defect: it is a path-level upper bound containing ancestors escalation declined to rewrite. Phase C verifies each staged blob digest against the manifest after git add, with lane mismatch a hard board_state_pending and shared mismatch a dropped shared_plane_deferred. Shared-plane paths are never in the phase A snapshot and never cause board_delta_moved. A whole-window CAS spanning step 6 is a defect, not an option. 17. The step-6 write set is planned, recorded, then verified, and the planner is the production walk rather than a second copy of it. planned_write_set is progress_path(txn.transition_element_id) union the progress paths of the ancestors a dry run of recalculateAncestors reports, intersected with board_paths(txn.story_id). The dry run and the real walk MUST be the same code path parameterized by a different progress writer, because two copies of the escalation predicate at pkg/board/escalation.go:127-170 would drift and the AC 16 equality assertion would then fail on correct behavior. Absence of step6_write_set is never treated as an empty set: a transaction at git_integrated_board_pending has no write set AND provably no durable transition, since 6c runs only after 6b's fsync, so recovery re-plans at 6a and additionally refuses txn_transition_foreign if the transition element is already done; a malformed or unreadable transaction record is integration_indeterminate, never an empty write set that would vacuously satisfy phase B. 18. Manifest membership is computed by the orchestrator from immutable transaction fields and never from any written record: board_paths(txn.story_id) intersected with dirty-relative-to-HEAD, passing AC 15 admission, and contained in txn.precondition_delta union step6_projection(txn). step6_projection is keyed to txn.transition_element_id and NOT to story_id, because a Story can finish through a Task, a Bug or a direct Story transition and the production call recalculateAncestors(b, store, b.ParentOf(elem), elem.ID()) at pkg/board/consistency.go:86 walks that element's own parent chain; it is recomputed as progress_path(transition_element_id) union the progress paths of its ancestors, intersected with board_paths(txn.story_id), and it is a sound upper bound because escalation writes an ancestor only when its aggregate target differs. It is used for membership only and never as the phase-B bound. transition_element_id is resolved from the accepted story_final CR before the transaction opens and is validated at open and at EVERY recovery to be that CR's final unresolved leaf, or the Story itself for a direct Story transition, and to sit in txn.story_id; failure is txn_transition_binding_invalid and refuses, and recovery must never fall back to a Story-wide projection on an invalid binding. The bound has TWO NESTED PARTS that must be tested separately: the outer board_paths(txn.story_id) boundary and the inner precondition_delta union step6_projection(txn); a test that only mutates a path in another Story reaches the outer part alone and cannot see a mutant that discards the inner intersection. The board write journal is not read for membership. When a frozen manifest exists, recovery recomputes and asserts equality, refusing board_manifest_indeterminate on mismatch. No-widen is a path-set bound, not an instant claim: the committed path set is contained in board_paths(txn.story_id), while content is whatever the store renders at freeze or recovery time, and this narrower claim must be stated in the implementation docs rather than overclaimed. 19. Negative evidence for AC 15 through AC 18 is mandatory and must drive the real integrate entry point. Design matrix rows N1, N2, N3, N3b, N3c, N4 and N5; rows 1i, 2, 2p, 2q, 2r, 2s, 2t, 3, 3b, 3c, 5, 6, 6a, 7i, 8, 11, 12 and the integration half of 10; and specifically row 3a, the outer-bound negative: after killing integrate between the durable done transition and the manifest freeze, read the durable txn_id, perform a legal board mutation on a path outside board_paths(STORY-A), hand-build a well-formed applied journal record carrying that stolen txn_id whose digest matches and whose bytes the store renders, then resume through real recovery; the path must be absent from both the recovered manifest and the commit; row 3a reaches only the OUTER bound. Row 3b is mandatory and reaches the INNER bound: after the same row-2 kill, run task-board m set_notes on a Story-A Task that is neither transition_element_id nor an ancestor of it and whose path is not in precondition_delta, forge an applied record carrying the stolen txn_id, and resume through real integrate; that Task's progress.md must be absent from the recovered manifest and from the board commit and must still be dirty in the worktree, and the target is provably outside both inner terms because set_notes writes only the named element's progress.md and triggers no ancestor escalation per pkg/board/query/mutations.go:1067-1092. Row 3c is mandatory: rewrite the durable txn.transition_element_id to an element in another Story, and separately to a same-Story element that is not the accepted CR's final leaf, and recovery must refuse txn_transition_binding_invalid without staging, committing or projecting. Rows 2p and 2q are mandatory kill-point rows for the transaction ordering: 2p kills between the step-4 transaction fsync and the step-5 advance and asserts a prepared record carrying expected_trunk_oid, candidate_commit_oid and transition_element_id, trunk equal to expected_trunk_oid, no board mutation and nothing staged, with BOTH resume and rollback asserted; 2q kills between the ff-only advance and the phase fsync and asserts that recovery decides from the recorded OIDs, treats it as git_integrated_board_pending, completes step 6 and step 7 exactly once with no second commit and no lost transition, and refuses integration_indeterminate on a third trunk value. Row 2r is MANDATORY and is the architecture revision 9 F1 regression: place a lane path p in precondition_delta, mutate p during step 5 to different bytes the store does render, let sub-step 6c become durable, kill integrate before the freeze, and resume through the real entry point; the recovered freeze must refuse board_delta_moved against the durable step6_write_set with nothing staged, no second commit and no replayed mutation, WHILE ROW 2, the identical kill with no drift, STILL SUCCEEDS in the same suite, because a recovery path that refuses both is refusing recovery rather than enforcing the gate. Row 2s asserts that absence of a write set is not emptiness, and row 2t forces a board mutation between 6b and 6c and requires txn_write_set_divergence with nothing staged or committed. Rows 5 and 6 are POSITIVES under architecture revision 8: a legal cross-lane write and a legal operator write that the store renders must be admitted and committed, not refused, and a suite that still refuses them is testing the withdrawn model. 20. The narrowing mutants are mandatory. Comparing candidates against the journal digest instead of the store rendering must break N1 and N2; restoring a whole-window equality CAS must break P1; widening phase B to admit any lane change must break N3b; moving the transaction open back to after step 5, the architecture revision 7 and 8 ordering, must break rows 2q and N3; widening manifest membership from precondition_delta union step6_projection(txn) to all of board_paths(txn.story_id) must break row 3b WHILE ROWS 3 AND 3a STILL PASS, which is the asymmetry the cycle-8 review identified; and keying step6_projection to txn.story_id instead of txn.transition_element_id must break rows 3b and 3c. TWO FURTHER MUTANTS narrow the durability of the phase-B bound and must leave the live-path rows green, which is the asymmetry the cycle-9 review identified: dropping step6_write_set from the transaction and falling back to step6_projection(txn) on the recovery path must break rows 2r and N3c while P1, N3b and row 2 still pass; and moving the step6_write_set fsync from sub-step 6b to 6d, after the mutation, must break rows 2r and 2s at the 6c-to-6d kill point. A delete-only mutant is not accepted as evidence for any of these, and deleting phase B outright cannot discharge them because it also breaks N3b and therefore cannot distinguish the live binding from the recovered one. 21. Integrate refuses a remote board (design matrix row 13ii) with worktree_isolation_requires_local_board before the integration lock and before the transaction opens: no journal transaction, nothing staged, HEAD unchanged, no board mutation replayed. The rationale recorded is data locality, not authority: no single process holds both operands of the admission comparison, and there is no tracked board tree for the board-state commit to record. 22. A whole-Story zero-repository-delta integrate (design matrix row 14ii) creates no Story commit, still runs the board mutation and the board-state commit so trunk gains exactly the board-only commit, and still cleans up. 23. Board mutation failure, concurrent Story landing, conflict, dirty checkout, crash-recovery, commit-time, and gate-order tests are deterministic; CLI, config and docs for this slice are updated. 24. The ordering in AC 11 and AC 16 is itself a tested contract, not a comment: named tests assert that the durable transaction record exists on disk with its full immutable identity BEFORE trunk moves, that step6_write_set is on disk BEFORE the status mutation writes its first byte, and that rollback is offered in exactly one phase, prepared with trunk unmoved, while every later phase resumes forward and none undoes a landed commit. 25. Recovery from board_transition_pending decides whether sub-step 6c ran by CLASSIFYING DURABLE CONTENT and NEVER by reading a status. step6_write_set carries, per path, class plus pre_digest plus post_digest, where pre_digest is sha256 of the store rendering before the mutation, the same rendering function admission and phase B already use, and post_digest is the serialization the recording dry-run writer is handed instead of writing. Recovery reacquires the board mutation lock and classifies each entry as PRE when the current rendering equals pre_digest, POST when it equals post_digest, ALIEN otherwise, and INDETERMINATE when the rendering cannot be produced or read. The decision ranges over lane_plan, the lane-class entries. All PRE re-plans, asserts the replan equals the record, and applies 6c. All POST DISCHARGES the 6c post-state assertion rather than skipping it, then advances. A mix of PRE and POST resumes the escalation walk EXACTLY ONCE and re-classifies; reaching all POST continues, and any residual PRE is txn_write_set_divergence, so the rule terminates. ALIEN on progress_path(transition_element_id) is txn_transition_foreign; ALIEN on any other entry is board_delta_moved. INDETERMINATE is integration_indeterminate and MUST NOT be silently classified PRE, because a failed or partial read is not an absence. An empty lane_plan or an unreadable record is integration_indeterminate and NEVER vacuously satisfies the all-POST test. The classifier proves exact planned post-state and NOT writer identity, and that limit is a REQUIREMENT rather than an apology: an identical foreign operation renders the identical bytes, classifies every lane entry POST, and MUST BE ADOPTED, because the transaction's postcondition is that the board holds this state and it does. Requiring a refusal from that construction is satisfiable only by reintroducing the writer-identity model design section 6.3.2a withdrew, and is the architecture revision 11 defect. Reading status == done here is the architecture revision 10 defect: a foreign mover can produce done while the crashed process holds no lock, and a 6c that applied its mutation and then failed its assertion leaves the identical durable phase, so the retry skipped the assertion that had just failed. 26. Every plan entry is a genuine state change and this is enforced, not assumed. pre_digest must differ from post_digest for every entry, which holds by construction because SetStatus writes the primary element only when its status changes, recalculateAncestors writes an ancestor only when target is non-empty and differs from current.Status after validateAutomaticStatusChange at pkg/board/escalation.go:127-170, and status is rendered into the Status heading. Sub-step 6b refuses txn_plan_degenerate if any entry violates it, because an entry that cannot be classified reintroduces exactly the ambiguity AC 25 removes. lane_plan is never empty in a correct run, since progress_path(transition_element_id) and the Story progress.md are both lane-class. 27. A refusal reached inside the transition is DURABLE BEFORE IT IS REPORTED. txn_write_set_divergence, txn_transition_foreign, txn_plan_degenerate and integration_indeterminate reached at or after sub-step 6b are each fsynced as refusal, carrying code, path, observed digest and expected value, together with the phase advance to transition_refused. That phase is TERMINAL TO EVERY AUTOMATIC PATH: recovery, retry, integrate, worktree repair, worktree gc and cleanup all re-report the recorded refusal verbatim, perform NO re-evaluation on any path, stage nothing, land no board commit and prune nothing. It is left ONLY through the AC 31 operator disposition surface, and a phase declared terminal with no defined exit is the architecture revision 11 F2 defect. A refusal that a retry can clear is not a refusal, and leaving the transaction at board_transition_pending after a divergence is the architecture revision 10 defect. 28. The transition lease is implemented on the board mutation surface and AUTHORIZES NOTHING. While a transaction sits at board_transition_pending or transition_refused, any mutation whose own write set intersects that transaction's LANE entries refuses element_under_integration, naming the transaction, the phase and the offending paths, unless the caller presents the matching txn_id. The lease is not a new record, because the transaction is the lease; intersection is decided by the SAME 6a dry-run planner rather than by a second predicate; it is scoped to lane entries and never to shared-plane aggregates, because leasing an Epic aggregate would freeze every concurrent lane behind one crashed integration; and it NEVER expires on a timer, because a TTL reintroduces the window it closes, so a crashed transaction holds its lane paths until integrate resumes or an operator abandons it, surfaced by worktree status. The token is caller-supplied exactly like commit_ack and MUST NOT be documented or implemented as unforgeable: NO GATE DEPENDS ON THE LEASE. The AC 25 classifier is the gate and consults no caller-supplied input; the lease is availability, so a crashed transaction does not turn every legal neighbouring mutation into a refusal. On a remote board the predicate is constantly false and the check is a no-op, which MUST BE STATED in the implementation docs rather than left implied, because an unstated no-op on one surface is a silent bypass. 29. Negative evidence for AC 25 through AC 28 is mandatory and drives the real integrate entry point. Row 2u forces txn_write_set_divergence at 6c AFTER the mutation is durable and then RETRIES: the first run records refusal and transition_refused before reporting, and the retry re-reports the identical code and evidence, re-evaluates nothing, stages nothing, lands no board commit and performs no cleanup. Row 2v kills integrate after 6b and before 6c, then runs a real foreign set_status on the transition leaf, which must refuse element_under_integration and write nothing, AND runs a real set_notes on an element whose write set is disjoint from the leased lane paths, which MUST SUCCEED, because a lease that blocks unrelated work is an outage rather than a gate and this half is mandatory; the resume then completes normally. Row 2w drives a genuinely foreign post-state under the lease-removal mutant: a real foreign set_status on the transition leaf followed by a set_notes on the same leaf, which renders bytes equal to neither digest, so the transition entry classifies ALIEN while the ancestors classify POST and the resume must refuse txn_transition_foreign into transition_refused with nothing staged or committed; its second half moves that second write to the Story, giving ALIEN on the Story ancestor entry and a board_delta_moved refusal with the same postconditions, which is the classifier's other ALIEN branch and had no row at all before. set_notes writes only the named element's progress.md and triggers no ancestor escalation per pkg/board/query/mutations.go:1067-1092, which is what makes the post-state provably foreign rather than merely different. Row 2wi is the MANDATORY POSITIVE half and repeats exactly row 2v's foreign set_status and nothing else under the same mutant: every lane entry classifies POST, recovery discharges the 6c post-state assertion and advances, and the integration completes with exactly one board commit and no replayed mutation. A suite that refuses row 2wi is enforcing writer identity. Both rows are EXPLICITLY CONDITIONAL ON THE MUTANT, because with the lease live no foreign write lands at all, which is the intended state. Row 2x kills integrate INSIDE the ancestor escalation walk between the leaf write and the Story aggregate write and requires a mixed classification, a single walk resume, all POST on re-classification and exactly one board commit, plus the variant where a planned lane path is still unwritten after that single resume and must give txn_write_set_divergence. Row 2y makes render(p) fail or return partially for one planned lane path and requires integration_indeterminate with the entry NOT classified PRE. Row 2z truncates step6_write_set to empty and separately to shared-class entries only and requires integration_indeterminate in both cases. 30. Four further narrowing mutants are mandatory and each MUST leave P1, row 2, row 2r and row 2t GREEN, because a suite that cannot tell a correct recovery from a credulous one is the suite architecture revision 10 shipped. Collapsing transition_refused back into board_transition_pending, reporting the refusal without fsyncing it, must break row 2u. Deciding whether 6c ran by status == done while leaving pre_digest and post_digest recorded but unread, which is architecture revision 10's behavior exactly, must break rows 2w, 2x and 2y. Removing the transition-lease check from the board mutation path must break row 2v's refusal half while 2v's discrimination half and every other row still pass, and rows 2w and 2wi must then both become reachable and both pass, 2w on the classifier's two ALIEN branches and 2wi on the honest all-POST adoption. Row 2wi must also stay GREEN under the status == done mutant, because it is a positive whose correct outcome that weaker observation happens to agree with, which is exactly why a suite of positives cannot find the revision 10 defect. Classifying an unreadable planned path as PRE rather than INDETERMINATE must break row 2y. A delete-only mutant discharges none of these, because deleting the classifier outright also breaks row 2 and therefore cannot distinguish a recovery that verifies the post-state from one that assumes it. 31. The operator disposition surface of design section 6.3.4e is the ONLY exit from transition_refused and integration_abandoned, and it is forward-only: no command in it undoes a landed commit or rewrites trunk. Three commands exist, worktree transaction show, resolve and discharge. All three refuse before writing anything unless the board is local (worktree_isolation_requires_local_board), the caller holds the repository integration lock and the Story lease in the control root (integration_blocked), TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID is ABSENT from the environment (transaction_disposition_not_operator), the transaction is in the phase the command accepts (txn_not_refused or txn_not_abandoned), and --refusal equals sha256 of the durable refusal record as stored (txn_refusal_digest_mismatch). NEITHER --refusal NOR the TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID check authorizes anything: both are caller-supplied guardrails exactly like commit_ack and the lease token, and they MUST NOT be implemented or documented as unforgeable. resolve --resolution repaired re-runs the AC 25 classifier under the board mutation lock and decides on that and NEVER on the operator's assertion: every lane entry POST fsyncs resolution and the advance to board_state_pending in ONE fsync and integration continues on the ordinary path, while anything else is txn_repair_incomplete with the phase unmoved, the original refusal left authoritative, and the lease still held. resolve --resolution incomplete-integration advances to the terminal phase integration_abandoned and NEVER deletes the record, NEVER rewrites trunk, creates no board-state commit, and keeps cleanup and worktree gc refused so the workspace stays visible and un-prunable; integrate then refuses story_integration_abandoned on EVERY CR revision for that Story, not merely on this transaction's key. The lease IS released at that point, and it is released EXPLICITLY AND ON THE RECORD, written into the resolution and reported by worktree status: the lease protects the classifier's decision inputs across a crash, no further classification will ever read step6_write_set at a terminal phase, and holding it would freeze the Story's lane paths forever for no property. What is prohibited is releasing it silently as a side effect of deleting a record, and that route does not exist. discharge is the only exit from integration_abandoned and is gated on the transaction's OWN postcondition, recomputed rather than claimed: for every lane entry of step6_write_set, HEAD must contain the path, the blob in HEAD must equal the store's current rendering, and that rendering must equal post_digest; all three for all entries retires the record to discharged and releases the lease, and anything else is txn_discharge_postcondition_unmet naming each failing entry and the condition it missed. Since .task-board is tracked, an abandoned Story's board state can reach trunk as an ordinary commit, which is what makes discharge reachable and integration_abandoned an operational state rather than a dead end. 32. Negative evidence for AC 31 is mandatory and drives the real command entry points. Row 2aa reaches transition_refused and then runs integrate, worktree repair, worktree gc and worktree cleanup in turn, each of which must re-report the recorded refusal verbatim without advancing the phase, staging a path, landing a board commit, deleting the transaction, releasing the lease or pruning the workspace or branch. Row 2ab attacks repaired with the board NOT at the planned post-state: a wrong --refusal digest gives txn_refusal_digest_mismatch with nothing written, the correct digest gives txn_repair_incomplete naming every non-POST entry with the phase unmoved, and a hand-written resolution plus phase board_state_pending written straight into the transaction file is re-classified on entry and refused txn_transition_not_in_place back into transition_refused; after a real repair through the sanctioned mutation surface presenting the txn_id, the same command MUST SUCCEED and the ordinary freeze and board commit must follow. Row 2ac abandons after the Story commit is on trunk and asserts present the record at integration_abandoned with the original refusal and reason, the Story commit with history unrewritten, and the workspace and branch; asserts absent any board-state commit and any deletion of the record; asserts refused cleanup, gc and integrate on any CR revision with story_integration_abandoned; and asserts worktree status reports integrated_board_uncommitted plus integration_abandoned with the reason and the explicit lease release. Row 2ad runs discharge before any lane path reaches trunk and after only some entries do, requiring txn_discharge_postcondition_unmet both times with nothing retired and cleanup still refused, then with every entry satisfying all three conditions requiring retirement to discharged and a succeeding cleanup, and finally hand-writes phase discharged with the postcondition unmet and requires cleanup to refuse txn_discharge_postcondition_unmet anyway because it recomputes. Row 2ae drives resolve at board_transition_pending and at integrated, discharge at transition_refused, either with TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID set, and either against a real remote-configured board, requiring txn_not_refused, txn_not_abandoned, transaction_disposition_not_operator and worktree_isolation_requires_local_board respectively with NOTHING WRITTEN in every case. 33. Five further narrowing mutants are mandatory and each MUST leave P1, row 2, row 2r and row 2t GREEN. Adding writer identity to the classifier must break row 2wi while row 2w still passes; this is the one mutant here that narrows a gate which is CORRECTLY permissive, and without it making the suite green and reintroducing the withdrawn authority model are the same move, which is the architecture revision 11 F1 defect. Making resolve --resolution repaired trust the operator instead of re-running the classifier must break row 2ab's txn_repair_incomplete case while row 2ab's final positive still passes, so it is not discharged by making repaired always refuse. Trusting the durable phase field on entry to board_state_pending i\\n[tool output bounded: strategy=head, original_bytes=86212, visible_bytes=40000]\\n<system-reminder>\\nFull output saved to: /Users/iv/.local/share/muse/sessions/2026/09/17/01a0ae20-8568-7b60-9562-eee7c66138af/tool-outputs/01a0ae2c-4816-7fb0-bbed-225002aee24d/call_01a0ae2c4306719dbfd3af