lify.yml\\ndocs\\nLICENSE\\nLOGBOOK.md\\nMakefile\\nNOTICE\\npkg\\nplanning\\nREADME.md\\nreferences\\nscripts\\nSKILL.md\\nSkillfile.json\\nSPEC.md\\ntask-board.config.json\\ntestdata\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/uncovered_gates_test.go:247:// `validation_suite_changed` — refuse outright.\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/integrate_matrix_test.go:220:\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"error = %v, want validation_suite_changed\\\", err)\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/integrate_matrix_test.go:224:\\t\\tt.Fatal(\\\"HEAD moved on validation_suite_changed\\\")\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/internal/integration/errors.go:90:\\tErrorValidationSuiteChanged ErrorCode = \\\"validation_suite_changed\\\"\\nBinary file /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/tools/board-cli/task-board matches\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260720-1fjsu9_board-workflow-and-spawn-policy-enhancements/STORY-260721-3er9sm_per-story-worktree-isolation-for-spawn/TASK-260803-kpx06r_implement-safe-story-squash-integration/progress.md:23:- [x] Implement tree-bound validation: refuse validation_not_bound_to_tree, validation_not_passing, validation_suite_changed, and validation_not_configured before any ref movement\\n/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/.task-board/EPIC-260720-1fjsu9_board-workflow-and-spawn-policy-enhancements/STORY-260721-3er9sm_per-story-worktree-isolation-for-spawn/TASK-260803-kpx06r_implement-safe-story-squash-integration/README.md:10:1. Before the final unresolved leaf producer starts, a clean short-lived Story checkpoint branch is refreshed to current trunk; conflicts are persisted and routed to same-branch rework, while success records the reviewed trunk OID. 2. The final leaf CR covers the complete Story candidate tree and integration refuses unless the latest evidence-backed accepted revision, candidate tree, and branch match by CAS and current trunk either equals reviewed_trunk_oid or re-parents onto it under AC 6. 3. task-board worktree integrate is orchestrator-only and creates exactly one single-parent commit with message keyed to Story plus CR, using repository Git identity and the accepted candidate tree; trunk advances only by ff-only. 4. Internal Task checkpoint commits are not preserved on trunk; no partial Story landing or application feature flag is allowed. 5. With version_control.confirm enabled, an explicit RFC3339 commit time is required, both author and committer dates equal it, the prose desired_commit_time and actual OID and time are recorded, and only post-Git board done uses commit_ack=scope_committed. 6. Acceptance invalidation is keyed to changed-path intersection, not trunk-OID equality. An intersecting advance routes to refresh, validation, and a new review revision. A non-intersecting advance re-parents in place through a three-way tree merge with base=base_oid, ours=trunk, theirs=candidate_tree_oid: a merge conflict, or a merged tree whose diff against trunk is not exactly changed_paths, demotes to stale; otherwise the CR keeps its revision and accepted state and emits a reparented audit event. A named test proves the accepted candidate tree is never committed under a moved trunk without that merge. 7. Validation evidence is bound to a tree OID, not to a CR and not to a commit. Integration refuses unless validation.tree_oid equals the candidate tree being committed (validation_not_bound_to_tree), validation.exit_status is zero (validation_not_passing), and validation.suite_sha256 equals the digest of the configured suite (validation_suite_changed). An unset worktree.validation.commands refuses with validation_not_configured before any ref movement; the gate defaults to refusing rather than to landing an unvalidated tree. 8. Because re-parenting sets a new candidate tree, it necessarily breaks the AC 7 binding and forces revalidation. A tree OID cannot be checked out: git worktree add --detach exits 128 with object is a tree, not a commit, reproduced on git 2.53.0. The merged tree is therefore materialized as the exact commit integration will land, by git commit-tree merged_tree -p trunk_oid with the resolved backdated author and committer dates; git rev-parse commit^{tree} must equal merged_tree; refs/task-board/revalidate/STORY-ID is created by an expected-old-value CAS against absent, both anchoring the commit against gc and refusing a leaked ref from a crashed attempt with revalidation_stale_ref rather than adopting it; the workspace is git worktree add --detach .temp/STORY-ID/revalidate at that commit; and the workspace HEAD^{tree} must equal merged_tree with a clean porcelain status before the suite runs. validation.tree_oid records merged_tree and never the materialized commit OID, which is retained as diagnostic context only. Teardown removes the workspace and deletes the ref on every exit path, and worktree gc prunes refs whose Story has no in-flight transaction plus any orphaned workspace. Revalidation runs inside the Story lease and the repository integration lock. Exit zero rebinds validation to the merged tree and preserves acceptance; a non-zero exit sets revalidation_failed and routes the element to to-dev with the log as an outcome resource, so the next handoff is a new CR revision requiring a new review; a suite or materialization that cannot execute sets revalidation_unavailable or revalidation_materialization_failed, neither of which is a pass or a rework signal, leaving integration blocked and retryable. revalidate_attempts is capped at 3 per accepted revision, after which the CR demotes to stale. When trunk has not moved again, trunk advances by ff-only to that same validated commit. 9. A named negative drives the real integrate entry point on a fixture where trunk advances with a signature change in path B while the accepted Story changes only its caller in path A, constructed so that path disjointness, the three-way merge, and the changed_paths equality check all pass. Validation must fail and the run must leave trunk unmoved, nothing staged in the control root, board status unchanged, no git_integrated_board_pending transaction phase, and the CR at revalidation_failed. 10. The class is proven by narrowing, not by deletion. Rebinding the AC 7 precondition from validation.tree_oid to validation.cr_id plus revision must make the AC 9 negative fail. Additionally, deriving validation.tree_oid from the materialized workspace's own HEAD^{tree} instead of asserting equality with merged_tree must make design matrix rows V1 and V2 fail: V1 pre-creates a stale refs/task-board/revalidate/STORY-ID pointing at an unrelated commit and requires revalidation_stale_ref with no suite run and no recorded pass; V2 makes materialization yield a workspace that is not the tree under test and requires revalidation_unavailable. A delete-only mutant is not accepted as evidence for any of these. 11. There is exactly ONE durable integration record, the IntegrationTxn keyed by story_id, cr_id and revision; the board write journal is a separate non-authorizing store-consistency mechanism that carries no integration phase and is never consulted by integration. The transaction is opened and fsynced in step 4, AFTER the phase-A closing re-read and STRICTLY BEFORE the step-5 ff-only trunk advance, which is the only irreversible act in the flow; step 1 builds the candidate commit through git commit-tree, which moves no ref. It carries the immutable identity story_id, cr_id, cr_revision, transition_element_id, expected_trunk_oid, candidate_tree_oid, candidate_commit_oid, repository_delta_empty, changed_paths, resolved_commit_time, phase_a_snapshot and precondition_delta, plus step6_write_set written once at sub-step 6b and refusal written at most once, and ONE monotonic NINE-phase ladder prepared, git_integrated_board_pending, board_transition_pending, transition_refused, integration_abandoned, board_state_pending, integrated, cleanup_pending, discharged, each advance fsynced before the next step. NO PHASE IS ENTERED ON THE STRENGTH OF THE RECORD THAT NAMES IT: entry to board_state_pending re-classifies lane_plan and refuses txn_transition_not_in_place into transition_refused on any residual PRE, and cleanup at discharged recomputes the AC 31 discharge postcondition, so a hand-written phase field is a resume point and never a credential. Design section 6.3.4d is the SINGLE NORMATIVE SOURCE for that ladder and its per-phase recovery; every other statement of it in the design or in this AC is a derived view and section 6.3.4d governs on any disagreement. Recovery dispatches on the recorded OIDs: phase prepared with trunk equal to expected_trunk_oid is rollback-or-resume with nothing landed; phase prepared with trunk equal to candidate_commit_oid is treated as git_integrated_board_pending and completed exactly once; any third trunk value refuses integration_indeterminate and never adopts, forces or guesses. Retry is idempotent across every phase and across duplicate invocation. A zero-repository-delta Story still opens the transaction in step 4 with repository_delta_empty true and candidate_commit_oid null, skipping only steps 1 to 3 and step 5. 12. Cleanup removes the short-lived worktree and branch only after exact commit ancestry, Story done, a committed board record, clean workspace, and no active lease or RUN; force removal or deletion is never automatic. 13. The integration checkout is the control root and no other checkout is ever advanced. Integration refuses with typed evidence unless the control root is the repository main working tree, HEAD is attached, HEAD names the configured trunk branch, HEAD equals the reviewed OID, the trunk branch is checked out in no other linked worktree, and no merge, rebase or cher