{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf1b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae20-8568-7b60-9562-eee7c66138af"},"sequence":1512,"recorded_at":1780531400003019,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"298248eb-2a9d-4aad-8474-d54f3cbb9bfa"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Review complete — **ACCEPTED**. `CR-TASK-260917-3lt2xv-1` rev1 is accepted and `TASK-260917-3lt2xv` routed to `integrating`.\n\nWhat was verified independently (all destructive probes in isolated copies; live worktree untouched, still uncommitted with exactly the 7 candidate paths at base `62d44630`):\n\n- **Contract**: `catalog.Adopted` is the single declaration with `Current()` defined through it; a planted `Current()→V050` divergence turns the pin test RED (exit 1). Adopted and explicit `-check` both exit 0; adopted, explicit, and committed outputs are byte-identical via `cmp`.\n- **Refusals** (each exit 1, distinct message, no output written): mixed flags, missing `-output`, missing derived metadata/lock (messages name the derived paths), v0.5.0-lock-under-adopted-name mismatch (pre-generation, no `generate catalog` wrap), same-length stale output under `-adopted -check` (file preserved, same as explicit form).\n- **Forward proof**: with `Adopted` planted to a fake release, `-adopted` derives the fake paths and applies the lock gate there — so consumer `n9r71p` only needs `Adopted = ReleaseV070` with matching files and keeps command 21 untouched.\n- **Config**: JSON walk shows exactly one changed string (command 21); **no-content diff** for `catalog_gen.go`/metadata/locks is empty.\n- **Mutation**: producer battery rerun in isolation — 8/8 narrowing KILLED + control SURVIVED; each KILLED rerun twice (16/16 exit 1). Own mutants: lock-derivation and mismatch-swallow both KILLED; mixed+`-check` weakening SURVIVES the committed suite but a behavioral probe proves the production gate refuses it (exit 1) while the mutant admits it (exit 0) — recorded as a non-blocking **P3** test-coverage note. No token-searching gate exists (grep exit 1).\n- **Validation**: commands 1–4 and 6–26 rerun green on the exact tree (full `go test ./...` and `-cover`: 26 ok; all 13 fuzz gates exit 0; `task-board validate` exit 0). Full `-race` accepted from the attached producer log (26 ok) plus a scoped `-race` rerun green here — stated explicitly.\n- **Integrate forecast**: `validation_suite_changed` will not refuse — `selectReviewedValidationSuite` (`tools/board-cli/.../integration/reviewed_suite.go`) expressly adopts a reviewed suite change when the CR is accepted with exit-0 evidence bound to the candidate tree, which holds here provided `task-board.config.json` is not edited after the evidence run.\n\nAttached before acceptance: `TASK-260917-3lt2xv_review-verdict-rev1.md` (8-of-8 AC table with call sites, exits, and rerun-vs-accepted statement) and `TASK-260917-3lt2xv_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` (real gzip, raw per-plant and per-command logs); reviewer checklist items 15–19 checked. Scratch copies deleted.","reason":null}}
